      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>7M NORTH OF 3 TIER LOG FENCE  

BCP621-CBP3
Elevation 1092.334 m
LOCATED ON HILL OVERLOOKING FISH CREEK PARK 7.0 M. N OF THREE TIER LOG FENCE AROUND PARK </groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1320756608">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-08-27T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP621 CBP3 [FOUND] (well, sort of)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I never expected to perform a CITO on a brass cap, but today was the day. After a couple of other misadventures in SW Calgary I found myself here. Aided by a helpful photo I swept where I thought I should, and came up with a buzz…and without too much effort pulled about 20% of a broken cap out of the dirt. Further sweeping in the nearby area produced no other buzzing. I don’t know what piece(s) of construction equipment performed this surgery in this location (or where the rest of it all is),  but it looks like I have an interesting memento.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="704098542">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP621 CPB3 [FOUND]

I began this morning with a plan to look for 4 caps In Fish Creek Provincial Park west of Macleod Trail and then look for another 4 in the park but east of Macleod Trail. This all unfolded according to plan. I still had a little time on my hands so decided to look for another pair in SE Calgary. I ended the day with a search for a geocache near the last cap. Thanks to ofth and vdD for setting up and maintaining these activities. I made a note of all the numbers and will add a few photos when I am near my photo software. This was brass cap #2 for today.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="686282758">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-14T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP621 CBP3

A Mother's Day family geobike in Fish Creek park fit the bill for today as an excuse to grab a few more caps and a caches in an area we don't get to too often. We park at 24th St SW and criss crossed the park up and down the hills that border the valley to grab the caps. Stopped for this as we got back to the car, the rest of the family waited at the bottom of the hill and I climbed for the the view and the find.

TFTC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682456106">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2500583">Count Smiley</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP621 CBP3&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cap provided the perfect opportunity for us to check out Bebo Grove.  We were supposed to come birding here earlier in the year but missed because of a scheduling conflict.  Really nice area and I look forward to returning for a more leisurely tour.  TFTCaps!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682409668">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP621 CBP3

We couldn't locate this one last summer due to the deep grass so came back this time armed with the metal detector.  We spotted the cap easily this time and didn't even turn the metal detector on.  TFTCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
